<section id="potential-issues-with-the-k-means-algorithm" class="level3">
<h3 class="anchored" data-anchor-id="potential-issues-with-the-k-means-algorithm">Potential issues with the <em>k</em>-means algorithm</h3>
<section id="the-globally-optimal-result-may-not-be-achieved" class="level4">
<h4 class="anchored" data-anchor-id="the-globally-optimal-result-may-not-be-achieved">1 - The globally optimal result may not be achieved</h4>
<p>First, although the <em>k</em>-means algorithm is guaranteed to improve the result in each step, there is no assurance that it will lead to the <em>global</em> best solution. For example, if we use a different random seed in our simple procedure, we might get a poor result:</p>
<div id="cell-15" class="cell" data-quarto-private-1="{&quot;key&quot;:&quot;colab&quot;,&quot;value&quot;:{}}" data-outputid="de3ada0e-638f-4525-e04c-9a1d05656285" data-execution_count="6">
<div class="code-copy-outer-scaffold"><div class="sourceCode cell-code" id="cb6" style="background: #f1f3f5;"><pre class="sourceCode python code-with-copy"><code class="sourceCode python"><span id="cb6-1">centers, labels <span class="op" style="color: #5E5E5E;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">=</span> find_clusters(X, <span class="dv" style="color: #AD0000;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">4</span>, rseed<span class="op" style="color: #5E5E5E;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">=</span><span class="dv" style="color: #AD0000;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">0</span>)</span>
<span id="cb6-2">plt.scatter(X[:, <span class="dv" style="color: #AD0000;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">0</span>], X[:, <span class="dv" style="color: #AD0000;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">1</span>], c<span class="op" style="color: #5E5E5E;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">=</span>labels,</span>
<span id="cb6-3">            s<span class="op" style="color: #5E5E5E;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">=</span><span class="dv" style="color: #AD0000;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">50</span>, cmap<span class="op" style="color: #5E5E5E;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">=</span><span class="st" style="color: #20794D;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">'viridis'</span>)<span class="op" style="color: #5E5E5E;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">;</span></span></code></pre></div></div>
<div class="cell-output cell-output-display">
<div>
<figure class="figure">
<p><img src="https://paulusm.github.io/portfolio-demo-new/posts/clustering/SK6_Clustering_files/figure-html/cell-7-output-1.png" width="537" height="417" class="figure-img"></p>
</figure>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<p>Here the <em>k</em>-means algorithm has converged, but has not converged to a globally optimal configuration. For this reason, it is common for the algorithm to be run for multiple starting guesses, as indeed Scikit-Learn does by default (set by the <code>n_init</code> parameter, which defaults to 10).</p>
</section>
<section id="the-number-of-clusters-must-be-selected-beforehand" class="level4">
<h4 class="anchored" data-anchor-id="the-number-of-clusters-must-be-selected-beforehand">2 - The number of clusters must be selected beforehand</h4>
<p>Another common challenge with <em>k</em>-means is that you must tell it how many clusters you expect: it cannot learn the number of clusters from the data. For example, if we ask the algorithm to identify six clusters, it will happily proceed and find the best six clusters:</p>
<div id="cell-18" class="cell" data-quarto-private-1="{&quot;key&quot;:&quot;colab&quot;,&quot;value&quot;:{}}" data-outputid="c49819f2-ebf2-498f-b43d-ff9bf8b4728d" data-execution_count="7">
<div class="code-copy-outer-scaffold"><div class="sourceCode cell-code" id="cb7" style="background: #f1f3f5;"><pre class="sourceCode python code-with-copy"><code class="sourceCode python"><span id="cb7-1">labels <span class="op" style="color: #5E5E5E;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">=</span> KMeans(<span class="dv" style="color: #AD0000;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">6</span>, random_state<span class="op" style="color: #5E5E5E;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">=</span><span class="dv" style="color: #AD0000;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">0</span>).fit_predict(X)</span>
<span id="cb7-2">plt.scatter(X[:, <span class="dv" style="color: #AD0000;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">0</span>], X[:, <span class="dv" style="color: #AD0000;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">1</span>], c<span class="op" style="color: #5E5E5E;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">=</span>labels,</span>
<span id="cb7-3">            s<span class="op" style="color: #5E5E5E;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">=</span><span class="dv" style="color: #AD0000;
background-color: null;
